django-admin.py startapp conferences

Add a conference through the admin (the "short title" should match "XXX" in
the URL used for this conference: exomol.com/conferences/XXX/ e.g.
exomol.com/conferences/ExoMol2018/

Create a "Rich text page": Conference "Spectroscopy of Exoplanets" under
"Activities" in the Mezzanine Pages admin (exomol.com/admin/pages/page/); in
its Meta data entry, make the URL "conferences/ExoMol2018". If the original
URL has already been sent out, let me know and I'll add a redirect.

Add child Rich text pages to it as necessary (venue, accommodation, speakers,
dates, letters, links, travel, ...)

Two features will require special attention: a form for registration and
abstract / presentation upload:

(1) Add a "Form" child page to the ExoMol2018 conference page and give it the
title "Registration". The "Content" is the preamble to the registration form;
the Response is the page shown after the user has submitted the form. Build
the form by adding and customizing Fields from the section at the bottom of
this admin page. You can also define an email to be sent when the form is
submitted.

(2) Abstract / presentation upload requires integration with the Django app:
I'll dig out the necessary files and implement them within the Mezzanine
framework of the current ExoMol website.

For now, I've marked the additional Mezzanine pages as Draft (ie only visible
on the live website by staff). You'll want to set this to Published when you're
happy with them.
